d access.\n62\t\n63\t**How to verify:** 1) Open authorization code for delegated actions. 2) Check it decides on the original subject and the current actor. 3) Answer no if it grants access because of any earlier actor in the chain (nested `act` claims, parent identity) or a union of chain permissions.\n64\t\n65\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n66\t\n67\t**Reviewer's note:** Exchange uses the workload token as subject and puts patient in the scope string, not the original subject as sub\n68\t\n69\t(no evidence cited)\n70\t\n71\t## E08.3\n72\t\n73\t**Check:** An action the parent was denied is also denied when routed through a more powerful peer, unless it carries its own explicit approval.\n74\t\n75\t**How to verify:** 1) Find how a parent asks a peer or child to act. 2) Check the request carries the parent's limits and the peer re-checks them, or requires its own explicit approval. 3) Answer no if a peer acts with its own wider permissions on a parent's request without that check.\n76\t\n77\t**Reviewer's evidence:** src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:44 — \"scope: `eligibility:read clinic:${clinicId} patient:${patientId}`,\"\n78\t\n79\t**Reviewer's note:** Peer cannot act for the parent\n80\t\n81\t`src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` lines 32–56 (cited lines marked >):\n82\t```\n83\t  32    }),\n84\t  33  });\n85\t  34  \n86\t  35  async function exchangeToken(workloadToken: string, clinicId: string, patientId: string): Promise<string> {\n87\t  36    const res = await fetch(env.tokenExchangeUrl, {\n88\t  37      method: \"POST\",\n89\t  38      headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" },\n90\t  39      body: new URLSearchParams({\n91\t  40        grant_type: \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange\",\n92\t  41        subject_token: workloadToken,\n93\t  42        subject_token_type: \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt\",\n94\t  43        audience: \"eligibility-agent\",\n95\t  44>       scope: `eligibility:read clinic:${cl